course: dictionary
lesson: 12817
title: Embellish: decorating and adding details
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To embellish something is to make it more beautiful by adding decorations. «Mia embellished her birthday card with sparkly sequins and a red ribbon.» The card was already a card. The sequins and ribbon made it prettier.
explain: You can also embellish a story by adding exciting details. «Sam embellished his story and said the fish was as long as a bus.» Extra details can make a story fun, but when you embellish a story, the extra details are often not true.
explain: Be careful with real facts. Adding untrue details to a school report or a true account is dishonest, so do not embellish the truth. Tell what really happened.
fact: Embellish is a verb: embellish, embellishes, embellished, embellishing.
fact: «Embellish» means to make something more beautiful by adding decorations.
fact: «Embellish» can also mean to add extra details to a story, often ones that are not true.
fact: «Embellished with gold» means decorated with gold.
fact: In a real report, embellishing the truth is dishonest.
exercise: «The old picture frame was embellished with tiny gold stars.» What does embellished mean here? | Painted over in plain black | Broken into pieces | *Decorated to look more beautiful | Sold at a market
exercise: «Ben embellished his story by saying the fish was as long as a bus.» What is Ben doing to his story? | Telling the true story exactly as it happened | Cutting the story down to one line | *Adding exciting details that are not true
exercise: «The cake was embellished with strawberries and cream.» Find and copy the one word that tells you the cake was decorated. | cream | strawberries | *embellished | cake
test: «Lily embellished her bag with glitter and beads.» What does embellished mean? | Threw it away | Made it smaller | *Made it more beautiful with decorations | Took the beads off
test: Why should you not embellish the truth in a school report? | Because the truth is always boring | *Because a report must be honest and true | Because reports must rhyme | Because teachers cannot read long words
exam: «The author embellished the old tale with dragons and magic castles.» What did the author do to the tale? | Removed all the words | *Added extra exciting details | Shortened it to one line | Translated it into French
